# SQLite Patterns

## Migrations: append-only, versioned

```rust
const MIGRATIONS: &[&str] = &[M001_INITIAL, M002_NOTE_INDEX];

pub fn migrate(conn: &mut Connection) -> AppResult<usize> {
    conn.execute_batch("CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS _migrations(…)")?;
    // read applied versions → for each pending:
    let tx = conn.transaction()?;
    tx.execute_batch(sql)?;
    tx.execute("INSERT INTO _migrations VALUES (?1, ?2)", …)?;
    tx.commit()?;      // all-or-nothing per migration
}
```

Shipped migrations are immutable; fixes arrive as NEW entries. This app ships
two — inspect `src-tauri/src/db/mod.rs` and its idempotency test.

## Repository layer = the only SQL home

```rust
pub fn complete_lesson(conn: &Connection, track: &str, module_id: &str, lesson_id: &str) -> AppResult<bool> {
    Ok(conn.execute(
        "INSERT OR IGNORE INTO lesson_completions(track, module_id, lesson_id, completed_at)\n         VALUES (?1, ?2, ?3, ?4)",
        params![track, module_id, lesson_id, now()],
    )? > 0)
}
```

Prepared statements + bound params everywhere (string interpolation into SQL is
a greppable crime). Repos return DTOs — `rusqlite::Row` never crosses upward.

## Rows → serde DTOs → webview

```rust
#[derive(Serialize)] #[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]
ub struct NoteDto { id: i64, title: String, updated_at: i64 }
```

The camelCase rename keeps ONE naming convention across the bridge. Vue sees
typed interfaces from `src/types/domain.ts` mirroring these structs.

## Smells
- Raw SQL inside commands (leaks persistence into the adapter layer),
- Synchronous long queries blocking commands (keep them indexed/fast; heavy work
  goes to spawn_blocking),
- Leaking DB types (`Vec<Row>`) toward Vue — always map to DTOs first.

